{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "One of the eight basic Allomantic metals. An Allomancer burning it can Riot, inflaming the emotions of people nearby.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "final-empire", "chapter": "7" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "A metal used by all three metal-based arts. Allomancers burn it to Riot emotions, Feruchemists store mental speed in it, and Hemalurgic spikes of zinc steal emotional fortitude.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "final-empire", "chapter": "7" },
            { "book": "well-of-ascension", "chapter": "50" },
            { "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "prologue" },
            { "book": "alloy-of-law", "chapter": "prologue" },
            { "book": "bands-of-mourning", "chapter": "3" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Rioting can strengthen desire, determination, anger and the like, and Rioting every emotion but one works much like Soothing that one. A Rioter cannot Riot themselves.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "well-of-ascension", "chapter": "46" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Very strong Rioting can take complete control of a Hemalurgic creature, and once it is controlled the Rioting is no longer needed. It takes a Mistborn burning duralumin with zinc, or several Rioters and Soothers together, though early in the Final Empire a single Rioter could do it.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "well-of-ascension", "chapter": "54" },
            { "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "21" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After the Catacendre, businesses may not use Rioters on their customers, but consensual Rioting is allowed, and some zinc counselors use it as a kind of therapy.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "alloy-of-law", "chapter": "2" },
            { "book": "shadows-of-self", "chapter": "14" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Feruchemist can store mental speed in zinc, turning slow-witted while filling it: words are heard at once but take longer to understand. Tapping it lets them think and reach conclusions very quickly, though it also makes them hungry.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "well-of-ascension", "chapter": "50" },
            { "book": "alloy-of-law", "chapter": "prologue" },
            { "book": "bands-of-mourning", "chapter": "3" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rioting is not mind control: it stirs emotions rather than dictating actions. It can be aimed at one person or a group, and at particular emotions, and is easier to aim in a direction than at a single person.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "final-empire", "chapter": "10" },
            { "book": "alloy-of-law", "chapter": "prologue" },
            { "book": "lost-metal", "chapter": "60" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
